{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 55, :comments ["<b>Only by lot shall the land be divided</b> among the tribes of Israel, and the names of the tribes of their fathers — they are twelve tribes — shall inherit them. And He returned and said: \"according to the lot shall their inheritance be divided\" — that of the tribe — \"between the many and the few,\" for also among the families they will cast a lot, and the portion of the Hanochite will be in whichever direction and place his lot comes up, and the portion of the Paluite in that same place which his lot comes up, but we will multiply for the many and diminish for the few among the families. And this is what is stated in the portion Mas'ei: \"And you shall possess the land by lot for your families; for the many you shall increase their inheritance, and for the few you shall diminish their inheritance; to whatever place the lot comes out for him, to him it shall be; by the tribes of your fathers you shall possess it\" (Numbers 33:54). Here He explained that the inheritance will be for the families by lot toward the direction in which the lot falls for him; there we will multiply for the many and diminish for the few among the families. And He said it will be \"by the tribes of their fathers,\" meaning twelve tribes. And what Rashi wrote (Rashi on Numbers 26:53): \"'for the names of the tribes of their fathers' — these are those who went out of Egypt\" — is not correct, for \"tribes\" (mattot) means only the tribes of Israel, twelve, as in the matter written: \"And no inheritance shall turn about from one tribe (mattah) to another tribe (mattah), but the tribes (mattot) of the children of Israel shall each cleave to his own inheritance\" (Numbers 36:9), and likewise \"a thousand for the tribe (mattah), for all the tribes (mattot) of Israel\" (Numbers 31:4), and likewise with the spies (above 13:2–15), and likewise everywhere. And there, shevet and mattah are one and the same. But what they said in the Gemara (Bava Batra 117a): Rabbi Yoshiya says: the land was divided to those who went out of Egypt, as it is said: \"for the names of the tribes of their fathers they shall inherit\" — this is a midrash of a redundancy in the verse, for it would have been enough to say \"only by lot shall the land be divided for the names of the tribes,\" and since it mentioned \"their fathers shall inherit,\" they darshened that the fathers — who are those mentioned in Egypt, \"these are the heads of their fathers' houses\" (Exodus 6:14) — are the ones who inherit the land, and from them it comes to those to whom it is apportioned."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:09:05.894418374Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}